s end-to-end; fabrication verified against real\nbinaries (claude 2.1.215, codex-cli 0.144.6) via planted-secret resume tests.\nVersion-pinned format specs live in turnbridge `docs/specs/`. Upstream\nconversation-ledger gained `package.json` exports + `gitUserIdentity` actor\nstamping (note: full transcript rescans can duplicate pre-identity events\nsince `actor.id` is part of the event-id hash).\n\nTwo non-obvious findings from the 2026-07-19 follow-up session:\n- **Codex TUI scrollback renders from `event_msg` records, not `response_item`.**\n  The model still SEES history from response_items (user confirmed resumed\n  Codex knew the prior context), but the screen looks empty without event_msg\n  `user_message`/`agent_message` twins. Codex fabrication now emits both;\n  shapes byte-match real rollout files.\n- **Bridging is a fork, not a move.** Fabricating a target session → target CLI\n  captures it as a NEW conversation under the id turnbridge generated (Codex\n  resume preserves the v4 id and appends). So both source and target show in\n  the picker — a real branch. Turnbridge records a `continuation` ledger event\n  (kind `continuation`, `links` rel `continues`, content `imported_through_seq`)\n  at fabricate time; picker labels lineage both directions and warns on\n  re-bridge. Default shows BOTH endpoints (no abandonment assumed). That edge\n  is also intent-recall's dedup key for the copied prefix. Related: [[evintunador-workflow-preferences]].\n","replaceAll":false,"structuredPatch":[{"lines":["   node_type: memory","   type: project","   originSessionId: c158a677-efd7-4ff4-87ac-1c3052566c2e","-  modified: 2026-07-21T21:40:46.956Z","+  modified: 2026-07-21T21:40:53.608Z"," ---"," "," Decisions made by the user on 2026-07-19 that override the original design docs:"],"newLines":7,"newStart":5,"oldLines":7,"oldStart":5},{"lines":[" stamping (note: full transcript rescans can duplicate pre-identity events"," since `actor.id` is part of the event-id hash)."," 