`readEvents` (to pull `conversation_turn` events, filtered by `kind` and `reachableFrom: \"HEAD\"`, in `src/conversations.ts:40-43` and `continuation`-kind events in `src/lineage.ts:70-73`), `sortEvents` (`src/conversations.ts:55`), `appendEvents` (to write its own `continuation` lineage events back into the ledger, `src/lineage.ts:35-51`), `findRepo` and `gitUserIdentity` (`src/resume.ts:1,147,152`), plus the `EvidenceEvent` and `RepoInfo` types throughout. Turnbridge writes exactly one kind of ledger event itself, `continuation` (`src/lineage.ts:3`), recording a `links: [{rel:\"continues\", target:&lt;source&gt;}]` edge each time it fabricates a cross-CLI session, so the picker can show \"→ bridged to X\" / \"↳ continued from Y\" annotations (`src/resume.ts:33-43`) — it never writes conversation content events. The main flow (`resumeCommand` in `src/resume.ts`) is: find the git repo, read the user's git identity, list/filter conversations by ownership and commit-reachability, let the user pick a conversation and a target CLI (interactively or via flags/config default), then build and run a `LaunchPlan` (same-CLI → native resume; cross-CLI → fabricate-then-fallback-to-bootstrap). An opt-in shim system (`src/shim.ts`) can rewrite `~/.zshrc` PATH to intercept bare `claude --resume`/`codex resume` invocations and redirect them into turnbridge's merged picker while passing everything else through untouched.\n\n## 4. Version assumptions about conversation-ledger baked into turnbridge\n\n- **Event kinds turnbridge reads/writes** (hard-coded string literals, not sourced from any shared enum in conversation-ledger):\n  - Reads `kind: \"conversation_turn\"` — `src/conversations.ts:41`.\n  - Reads/writes `kind: \"continuation\"` — `src/lineage.ts:3` (`CONTINUATION_KIND`), used in `readEvents(..., {kind: CONTINUATION_KIND})` (`src/lineage.ts:71`) and `appendEvents` (`src/lineage.ts:37`).\n  - Uses `links` rel value `\"continues\"` — `src/lineage.ts:4` (`CONTINUES_REL`), hard-coded string, matched against ledger's generic `links: EventLink[]` extension point (`conversation-ledger/src/schema.ts:92`).\n- **EvidenceEvent field shape assumptions** (from `conversation-ledger/src/schema.ts:74-108`, currently matching): `id`, `kind`, `occurred_at`, `actor {type, id, display}`, `producer {source, session_id, tool, version}`, `content`, `conversation {id, seq}`, `links`. Turnbridge assumes `actor.type` is one of `\"human\" | \"agent\" | \"system\"` (`src/conversations.ts:59`, `src/lineage.ts:39`, `src/targets/claude-code.ts:137,139`, `src/targets/codex.ts:134`) — this enum is not re-exported/typed from conversation-ledger's public API in what was read; it's an assumed convention.\n- **`readEvents` options API**: assumes support for `{kind, reachableFrom: \"HEAD\"}` filter shape (`src/conversations.ts:40-43`, `src/lineage.ts:70-73`) — matches `ReadOptions` type exported from conversation-ledger's `store.js`.\n- **`appendEvents` accepts an array of event drafts** with `kind`, `occurred_at`, `actor`, `producer`, `conversation`, `links`, `content` — assumes `conversation: {id, seq: 0}` is valid for a non-`conversation_turn` event type riding under an existing conversation id (`src/lineage.ts:36-51`); this is an implicit assumption about how conversation-ledger scopes/dedupes events by `conversation.id` for non-turn event kinds, not explicitly documented as tested in the repo's docs.\n- **`producer.source` / `producer.session_id` convention**: turnbridge derives CLI name and native session id from `producer.source` and `producer.session_id`, falling back to parsing the conversation id string (`id.split(\":\")`) when absent (`src/conversations.ts:66-67`) — implies an assumed id-namespacing convention (`&lt;source&gt;:&lt;session-id&gt;`) that isn't verified against conversation-ledger's actual id-generation code in this pass.\n- **Identity stamping is versioned/optional**: `docs/WIP_TECHNICAL_DESIGN.md:89-91` explicitly notes \"Events captured before identity stamping existed are unattributed; a forced transcript rescan after the upgrade can duplicate those turns under new event ids\" — a direct backward-compatibility assumption about older conversation-ledger-captured data.\n- **CLI-version pins are turnbridge's own, independent of conversation-ledger's version**, but gate fabrication safety: `VALIDATED_VERSION_PREFIX = \"2.\"` for Claude Code (`src/targets/claude-code.ts:17`) and `VALIDATED_VERSION_PREFIX = \"0.144.\"` for Codex (`src/targets/codex.ts:16`) — both are prefix checks against the *target CLI's* own version, not conversation-ledger's, but they're the operative \"version assumption baked in\" mechanism described in the WIP doc's \"Fabrication contract\" section (`docs/WIP_TECHNICAL_DESIGN.md:64-67`).\n- No explicit check anywhere in `src/` of conversation-ledger's own package `version` or a `SCHEMA_VERSION`/compatibility field at runtime — turnbridge's `package.json:33` pins the dependency only via `\"conversation-ledger\": \"file:../conversation-ledger\"` (a local path dependency, not a semver range), meaning compatibility is enforced only by co-development in this monorepo-like sibling-directory setup, with no runtime guard against a conversation-ledger schema change breaking turnbridge silently.</result>\n<usage><subagent_tokens>67475</subagent_tokens><tool_uses>30</tool_uses><duration_ms>122317</duration_ms></usage>\n</task-notification>","role":"user"},"origin":{"kind":"task-notification"},"parentUuid":"7f42f2cc-7f19-4e44-9a65-ec663916c351","permissionMode":"auto","promptId":"fdfc723a-e466-424f-9151-071edf2005d4","promptSource":"system","sessionId":"6b979ed9-e38e-4fea-b585-342bba5a333c","slug":"hazy-floating-cupcake","timestamp":"2026-07-21T21:23:03.042Z","type":"user","userType":"external","uuid":"0b775bd4-2cfb-4b2b-92e8-b57cb1d2803d","version":"2.1.216"},"format":"claude-code-jsonl/1"},"recorded_at":"2026-07-21T21:23:09.355Z","schema":"conversation-ledger/v1"}
{"actor":{"display":"Evin Tunador","id":"evintunador@gmail.com","type":"human"},"content":{"blocks":[{"text":"<task-notification>\n<task-id>a5c627b890fdc1883</task-id>\n<tool-use-id>toolu_014zVR3mNKPH7cTzVr3mT3Rq</tool-use-id>\n<output-file>/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-evintunador-repos-evintunador-turnbridge/6b979ed9-e38e-4fea-b585-342bba5a333c/tasks/a5c627b890fdc1883.output</output-file>\n<status>completed</status>\n<summary>Agent \"Diff cledger recent changes\" finished</summary>\n<note>A task-notification fires each time this agent stops with no live background children of its own. The user can send it another message and resume it, so the same task-id may notify more than once.</note>\n<result># Findings: conversation-ledger 0.5.0→0.9.0 vs turnbridge's 0.4.0 baseline\n\nRepo: `/Users/evintunador/repos/evintunador/conversation-ledger`, HEAD `8e6bf37` (2026-07-21), package.json version `0.9.0`. Only tag in repo is `v0.1.0`; all later versions identified via `package.json` bump commits, no annotated tags.\n\n## 1. Version → commit map (date, hash)\n\n| Version | Commit | Date | Subject |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| 0.4.0 (turnbridge's baseline) | `82fdd94` | 2026-07-19 | Transport hooks, git-native identity, drift detection |\n| 0.5.0 | `b3943c6` | 2026-07-20 | Preserve unrecognized transcript lines raw-only |\n| 0.6.0 | `6526090` | 2026-07-20 | Re-normalize preserved unrecognized events |\n| 0.6.1 | `54bb44b` | 2026-07-20 | Fully mask matched span in scan/sync findings |\n| 0.7.0 | `33f522b` | 2026-07-20 | Opt-in known-secrets store |\n| 0.7.1 | `1ddda10` | 2026-07-20 | Tighten keyword-assignment rule, lock store to 0600 |\n| 0.8.0 | `a452048` | 2026-07-20 | `cledger re-anchor` command (+ `d3934db` re_anchor events, `c36b4b5` auto-detect, all same-day cluster) |\n| 0.9.0 | `62757ac` | 2026-07-21 | Evidence-ranked suggestions (+ `61c9c89` forge abstraction, `695dad4` follow-up fix) |\n\n## 2. Per-release detail\n\n**0.5.0 — preserve unrecognized lines (`b3943c6`)**\n- New `unrecognized` event kind added to `KNOWN_KINDS` (`src/schema.ts`). Adapters (`claude-code.ts`, `codex.ts`, `drift.ts`) now emit an `unrecognized` event (content = `{unrecognized_type}` label, full source line in `raw.data`) instead of silently dropping unmapped transcript line types.\n- No new library exports. Behavior change (default-on, not opt-in): any `readEvents()` call without a `kind` filter will now see `unrecognized` events it never saw before. Downstream code that iterates all events without filtering by `kind` must tolerate this new kind.\n- Codex `reasoning`/encrypted blocks are explicitly excluded — policy unchanged.\n\n**0.6.0 — re-normalization (`6526090`)**\n- New library exports: `renormalize()`, type `RenormalizeResult` (`src/index.ts` diff, `src/renormalize.ts` new file).\n- New CLI command: `cledger renormalize`.\n- Turns preserved `unrecognized` events this cledger version can now parse into `conversation_turn` + appends a `supersession` event (`links:[{rel:\"supersedes\", target}]`). Id-fidelity: reconstructed turn gets the exact id a live capture would produce, so future live capture dedups.\n- Opt-in/manual only — must be invoked explicitly (`cledger renormalize`), not run automatically. Not a default-behavior change by itself, but its output (new `conversation_turn` + `supersession` events) is a new steady-state a reader must expect once someone runs it.\n\n**0.6.1 — mask matched span (`54bb44b`)**\n- Internal to `src/redact/scan.ts` (finding-report formatting only). No API/schema/CLI surface change. Not consumer-relevant.\n\n**0.7.0 — known-secrets store (`33f522b`)**\n- New config key `{\"redact\": {\"knownSecrets\": true}}`, opt-in/off by default. Local-only store at `.git/conversation-ledger/known-secrets.json`.\n- No new exported functions/types in `src/index.ts`. `cli.ts` and `store.ts`/`redact/apply.ts`/`redact/known-secrets.ts` touched internally.\n- Behavior note: enabling this makes capture machine-dependent for remembered values (different event ids on machines without the value cached) — same caveat as pre-existing env-masking.\n\n**0.7.1 — hardening (`1ddda10`)**\n- Tightens the sync-scan keyword-assignment regex (fewer false positives) and fixes 0.7.0's store perms (0600 enforced/repaired on write; previously landed 0644). No public API change.\n\n**0.8.0 — re-anchoring (`d3934db`, `c36b4b5`, `a452048`)**\n- **New event kind**: `re_anchor` added to `KNOWN_KINDS` (`src/schema.ts`, commit `d3934db`). A mapping event asserting rewritten-away commits (squash/rebase) live on in a successor commit. Anchored to the successor, deterministic id (sorted SHAs + system actor).\n- **New exports** (`src/index.ts`): `runReAnchor`, `manualReAnchor`, `defaultRewriteTarget`, `detectRewrites`, `parseReAnchor`, `reAnchorDraft`; types `ReAnchorRunResult`, `DetectedRewrite`, `DetectRewritesResult`, `ReAnchorMapping`, `ReAnchorDraftOptions`, `UnmatchedBranch`.\n- **New CLI command**: `cledger re-anchor` (dry-run default, `--apply`, manual `&lt;old-rev...&gt; --onto REV`).\n- **`appendEvents` signature change (additive, non-breaking)**: `opts: { context?: RepoContext }` → `opts: { context?: RepoContext; anchor?: string }` (`src/store.ts`). Optional param, source-compatible.\n- **`readEvents` reachability semantics changed**: previously `opts.reachableFrom` did plain `git rev-list` filtering; now (`resolveAnchors` in `store.ts`) it resolves `re_anchor` mappings to a fixpoint so squash-orphaned anchors \"revive.\" This is a **behavior change on default reads** — a downstream consumer's reachable-event set can now include events anchored to commits that are not actually reachable via plain git history, once a mapping exists.\n- **DEFAULT-ON SIDE EFFECT (important for turnbridge)**: `readEvents()` now also calls `autoReAnchor(repo)` (`c36b4b5`) on every invocation. This can **write** a `re_anchor` event to the git-notes ledger (via `appendEvents`) as a side effect of what turnbridge treats as a read-only call (`listConversations`, `readLineage` in turnbridge both call `readEvents`). Gated by a tip cursor file at `&lt;gitDir&gt;/conversation-ledger/reanchor-cursor` (only re-runs detection when the target branch's tip moved), never throws, and prints progress/ambiguity messages to `stderr`. Opt-out: `{\"reanchor\": {\"auto\": false}}` in `.cledger.json`/`~/.config/cledger/config.json`. New `CledgerConfig.reanchor` config section (`src/redact/config.ts`).\n- `SCHEMA_VERSION` string (\"conversation-ledger/v1\") was **not** bumped despite the new `re_anchor`/`unrecognized` kinds — kinds are treated as open/extensible, not schema-version-gated.\n\n**0.9.0 — evidence-ranked suggestions + forge abstraction (`62757ac`, `61c9c89`, `695dad4`)**\n- New files `src/forge/forge.ts`, `src/forge/github.ts`, `src/reanchor-suggest.ts`.\n- **New exports**: `suggestMappings`, `forgeForRepo`; types `BranchSuggestions`, `Suggestion`, `ForgeDriver`, `ForgePullRequest`.\n- `ForgeDriver.pullRequestsForBranch(branch)` — GitHub driver over the user's `gh` CLI session (no credential handling by cledger itself; 10s timeout; degrades to `null` rather than throwing on missing/unauthenticated `gh`, non-GitHub origin, offline).\n- `detectRewrites`/`UnmatchedBranch` extended to report non-exact matches (previously just dropped) with a `noted` commit subset (`695dad4` fix, so the confirm-command doesn't accidentally drop the anchor commit).\n- Forge lookups run **only** inside the explicit `cledger re-anchor` command, never in the automatic read-time path (`autoReAnchor` stays offline) — so this doesn't add new default-path network calls, but it does mean `cledger re-anchor` (interactive/manual use) can now shell out to `gh`.\n- Opt-out: `--no-forge` flag / `{\"reanchor\": {\"forge\": false}}`.\n- `695dad4` is a same-day follow-up bugfix to `62757ac`'s output (not a separate version bump).\n\n## 3. Breaking / behavior-changing items a consumer must react to\n\n1. **New event kinds `re_anchor` (0.8.0) and `unrecognized` (0.5.0), plus `supersession` usage growth (0.6.0)** — any code that enumerates `readEvents()` output without an explicit `kind:` filter must now tolerate these. Turnbridge is currently safe here: `src/conversations.ts` and `src/lineage.ts` both pass an explicit `kind` filter (`\"conversation_turn\"` / `CONTINUATION_KIND`) to `readEvents`, so these extra kinds are filtered out — **no actual code fix needed**, but worth confirming this remains true if turnbridge ever calls `readEvents` without a kind filter.\n2. **`readEvents()` now has write side effects (0.8.0, `c36b4b5`)** — every call may append a `re_anchor` event to the notes ref and always may write `&lt;gitDir&gt;/conversation-ledger/reanchor-cursor`, plus emit `stderr` diagnostics. Turnbridge calls `readEvents` from `listConversations` (`src/conversations.ts:40`) and `readLineage` (`src/lineage.ts:70`), both of which turnbridge likely treats as pure reads. This is the most concrete \"must react to\" item — turnbridge should decide whether to accept this (git-notes mutation + stderr noise on what look like read commands) or set `{\"reanchor\": {\"auto\": false}}`, and should surface/suppress the new stderr messages intentionally rather than let them leak into CLI output.\n3. **`reachableFrom` filtering semantics changed (0.8.0)** — no longer plain git reachability; now resolves through `re_anchor` mappings to a fixpoint. Turnbridge's `reachableFrom: \"HEAD\"` calls will silently start including events anchored to squash-rewritten-away commits once mappings exist. Functionally desirable (that's the point of the feature) but is a behavior change from what was integrated against at 0.4.0.\n4. **`appendEvents` new `anchor` option (0.8.0)** — additive/optional, non-breaking for existing call sites (turnbridge's `lineage.ts` call to `appendEvents(repo, [...])` with no third arg is unaffected).\n5. **New `CledgerConfig.reanchor` section (0.8.0)** — if turnbridge ever reads/writes `.cledger.json` itself, it should be aware of this new shallow-merged top-level section (same shallow-merge-per-section rule as `redact`/`scan`/`transport`).\n6. `SCHEMA_VERSION` (\"conversation-ledger/v1\") has **not changed** across 0.5.0–0.9.0 — no format-version gate to react to.\n7. No changes found to `git.ts` (`findRepo`, `gitUserIdentity`, `headSha`, `currentBranch`, `repoIdentity`, `git`, `GitError`) since 0.4.0 — turnbridge's `src/resume.ts` usage of `findRepo`/`gitUserIdentity` is unaffected.\n8. No changes to `ReadOptions` shape (`reachableFrom`, `kind`, `source`, `conversation`) since 0.4.0 — purely additive elsewhere.\n\n## 4. Installed copy at turnbridge/node_modules/conversation-ledger\n\n- `node_modules/conversation-ledger` is a **symlink** to `../../conversation-ledger` (the sibling repo itself, i.e. `npm install`'d as `file:../conversation-ledger`, effectively `npm link`-style).\n- Its `package.json` reports `\"version\": \"0.9.0\"`, matching the source repo's current `package.json`.\n- `dist/index.js` (built output) does export `suggestMappings` (`from \"./reanchor-suggest.js\"`) and `forgeForRepo` (`from \"./forge/forge.js\"`) — confirms `dist/` is built from current HEAD, not stale (`dist/index.js` mtime 2026-07-21 11:39, after `src/index.ts`'s last edit 2026-07-21 10:28).\n- `git status --short` in the cledger repo is clean; `dist/` is gitignored (build artifact, not tracked) but matches source.\n- Turnbridge's `package.json` declares `\"conversation-ledger\": \"file:../conversation-ledger\"`; `package-lock.json` reflects the same. So **turnbridge is always building/running against cledger's current HEAD (0.9.0)** via the symlink — there is no version pin lagging behind. The staleness is entirely in turnbridge's own code/docs not having been updated to use or account for the new API surface, not in a stale installed artifact.\n\n## 5. Turnbridge's own awareness (or lack thereof)\n\n- `git log --oneline -- package.json package-lock.json` in turnbridge: only one commit, the MVP (`49da723`) — no version-bump or integration commits since.\n- Grep across turnbridge source/docs for `re_anchor`, `reanchor`, `renormalize`, `unrecognized`, or any cledger version string: **zero hits** outside an unrelated match in `docs/specs/claude-session-format.md:99` (\"unrecognized wholesale\" — unrelated string).\n- Turnbridge's imports from `conversation-ledger` (all still valid, nothing removed): `src/conversations.ts:1` (`readEvents, sortEvents, EvidenceEvent, RepoInfo`), `src/lineage.ts:1` (`appendEvents, readEvents, EvidenceEvent, RepoInfo`), `src/types.ts:1` / `src/transcript.ts:1` (`EvidenceEvent` type only), `src/resume.ts:1` (`findRepo, gitUserIdentity, RepoInfo`), `src/test/helpers.ts:10`.\n- **Turnbridge's own docs are already stale, even relative to 0.4.0**: `docs/WIP_TECHNICAL_DESIGN.md:88-89` still says \"Transport is Conversation Ledger's explicit `cledger sync` (git notes push/fetch); turnbridge adds no network behavior\" — contradicted by cledger's 0.4.0 default-on pre-push/fetch transport hooks (and turnbridge's own `docs/PRODUCT_INTENT.md` was amended for this in commit `29a543f`, 2026-07-19, but `WIP_TECHNICAL_DESIGN.md` was never updated to match). Same doc, line 97, still calls \"ledger-side redaction... an open roadmap item,\" but redaction shipped in cledger 0.3.0 (`88dc79e`), predating even turnbridge's baseline integration.\n\n## 6. cledger's own roadmap (README.md, lines 174-260) — what's still unshipped, that turnbridge may be waiting on\n\n- **Path-based capture exclusion** (e.g. never record reads of `secrets/**`) — not started.\n- **Post-push purge** (true content removal after ledger ref is shared) — only the local pre-push squash via `cledger redact` shipped; full purge (force-push + collaborator coordination, resurrected-blob detection, host object-retention caveat) is explicitly unshipped, three sub-problems scoped but not built.\n- **Harness-artifact capture** (Claude Code auto-memory dirs, non-git-controlled session state) — undecided, not started.\n- **Format-drift auto-trigger**: `cledger renormalize` remains manual-only; auto-running it after an adapter/version bump is explicitly deferred (\"detecting 'the adapter changed' is its own problem\").\n- **Encrypt known-secrets store at rest** — only file perms (0600) shipped (0.7.1); OS-keychain-backed encryption (Keychain/libsecret/DPAPI) is unshipped, flagged as needing non-interactive decrypt since capture runs silently every turn.\n- **Sub-turn citation anchors** for downstream consumers like intent-recall — not started, directly relevant to the broader ecosystem turnbridge is part of.\n- **Forge (PR/MR) conversation adapter** — ingesting PR review comments as conversation events anchored to the merge/squash commit. The forge abstraction (`src/forge/`) now exists as a prerequisite (0.9.0), but comment-fetching itself is not built.\n- **Forge-side integration (CI/GitHub App)** — opt-in Action/webhook to append re-anchor mappings and push notes from CI at merge time; explicitly kept out of core, unshipped.\n\n**Items the roadmap marks as already shipped** (so turnbridge should NOT expect these as still-pending): `re-anchor` (0.8.0) and its suggestion tier (0.9.0); \"capture/scan redaction feedback loop\" (closed via 0.6.1 span-masking + 0.7.0 known-secrets store, with the \"capture-tier as strict superset of scan-tier\" framing explicitly rejected/deferred as a non-goal, not an oversight).</result>\n<usage><subagent_tokens>70860</subagent_tokens><tool_uses>39</tool_uses><duration_ms>251065</duration_ms></usage>\n</task-notification>","type":"text"}],"role":"user"},"context":{"branch":"main","cwd":"/Users/evintunador/repos/evintunador/turnbridge","head":"29a543fb82805e7dc0998709190735a9e002153e","repo":"git@github.com:evintunador/turnbridge.git"},"conversation":{"id":"claude-code:6b979ed9-e38e-4fea-b585-342bba5a333c","seq":47},"id":"ev1-ec17739a499b0ad8946b7cdd83c55d5c8cd2bf3de87122b7159788d24e544ef6","kind":"conversation_