 |\n| 0.9.0 | `62757ac` | 2026-07-21 | Evidence-ranked suggestions (+ `61c9c89` forge abstraction, `695dad4` follow-up fix) |\n\n## 2. Per-release detail\n\n**0.5.0 — preserve unrecognized lines (`b3943c6`)**\n- New `unrecognized` event kind added to `KNOWN_KINDS` (`src/schema.ts`). Adapters (`claude-code.ts`, `codex.ts`, `drift.ts`) now emit an `unrecognized` event (content = `{unrecognized_type}` label, full source line in `raw.data`) instead of silently dropping unmapped transcript line types.\n- No new library exports. Behavior change (default-on, not opt-in): any `readEvents()` call without a `kind` filter will now see `unrecognized` events it never saw before. Downstream code that iterates all events without filtering by `kind` must tolerate this new kind.\n- Codex `reasoning`/encrypted blocks are explicitly excluded — policy unchanged.\n\n**0.6.0 — re-normalization (`6526090`)**\n- New library exports: `renormalize()`, type `RenormalizeResult` (`src/index.ts` diff, `src/renormalize.ts` new file).\n- New CLI command: `cledger renormalize`.\n- Turns preserved `unrecognized` events this cledger version can now parse into `conversation_turn` + appends a `supersession` event (`links:[{rel:\"supersedes\", target}]`). Id-fidelity: reconstructed turn gets the exact id a live capture would produce, so future live capture dedups.\n- Opt-in/manual only — must be invoked explicitly (`cledger renormalize`), not run automatically. Not a default-behavior change by itself, but its output (new `conversation_turn` + `supersession` events) is a new steady-state a reader must expect once someone runs it.\n\n**0.6.1 — mask matched span (`54bb44b`)**\n- Internal to `src/redact/scan.ts` (finding-report formatting only). No API/schema/CLI surface change. Not consumer-relevant.\n\n**0.7.0 — known-secrets store (`33f522b`)**\n- New config key `{\"redact\": {\"knownSecrets\": true}}`, opt-in/off by default. Local-only store at `.git/conversation-ledger/known-secrets.json`.\n- No new exported functions/types in `src/index.ts`. `cli.ts` and `store.ts`/`redact/apply.ts`/`redact/known-secrets.ts` touched internally.\n- Behavior note: enabling this makes capture machine-dependent for remembered values (different event ids on machines without the value cached) — same caveat as pre-existing env-masking.\n\n**0.7.1 — hardening (`1ddda10`)**\n- Tightens the sync-scan keyword-assignment regex (fewer false positives) and fixes 0.7.0's store perms (0600 enforced/repaired on write; previously landed 0644). No public API change.\n\n**0.8.0 — re-anchoring (`d3934db`, `c36b4b5`, `a452048`)**\n- **New event kind**: `re_anchor` added to `KNOWN_KINDS` (`src/schema.ts`, commit `d3934db`). A mapping event asserting rewritten-away commits (squash/rebase) live on in a successor commit. Anchored to the successor, deterministic id (sorted SHAs + system actor).\n- **New exports** (`src/index.ts`): `runReAnchor`, `manualReAnchor`, `defaultRewriteTarget`, `detectRewrites`, `parseReAnchor`, `reAnchorDraft`; types `ReAnchorRunResult`, `DetectedRewrite`, `DetectRewritesResult`, `ReAnchorMapping`, `ReAnchorDraftOptions`, `UnmatchedBranch`.\n- **New CLI command**: `cledger re-anchor` (dry-run default, `--apply`, manual `&lt;old-rev...&gt; --onto REV`).\n- **`appendEvents` signature change (additive, non-breaking)**: `opts: { context?: RepoContext }` → `opts: { context?: RepoContext; anchor?: string }` (`src/store.ts`). Optional param, source-compatible.\n- **`readEvents` reachability semantics changed**: previously `opts.reachableFrom` did plain `git rev-list` filtering; now (`resolveAnchors` in `store.ts`) it resolves `re_anchor` mappings to a fixpoint so squash-orphaned anchors \"revive.\" This is a **behavior change on default reads** — a downstream consumer's reachable-event set can now include events anchored to commits that are not actually reachable via plain git history, once a mapping exists.\n- **DEFAULT-ON SIDE EFFECT (important for turnbridge)**: `readEvents()` now a